A node is a state whose pivot column has, on the window `0, …, w-1`, numerators given by a
pattern of affine forms in integer parameters (`WinPat`), and outside it numerators divisible
by `√2 ^ δ` (`TailD`); its goal is the join of `A = H_[1,3] H_[0,2]` and
`B = H_[1,3] H_[0,2] H_[0,1]` (`wJ`).  The entries `c34_entryE0`, …, `c34_entryN1` take the four
odd entries at `0, 1, 2, 3` with the classes `ε`, `1 - ε`, `ε`, `1 - ε` and the parity `η` of
`H_[0,1] s` at `0`; then, following Clément:

* Lemma 5.7 (`η = ε`, a transfer along `(-1)_[1]`), Lemma 5.9 (`ε = 1`, along
  `(-1)_[1] X_[0,1] X_[2,3]`) and Assumption 3 (signs on `2`, `3`);
* Subcase 3.4.1, the two reduced entries of one class: a path by (20);
* Subcase 3.4.2: the entries `e₄`, `e₅` of depth 1 forced by Lemma 2.1 (`tail_entry`), moved to
  `4`, `5` (`extend_entry`); Assumption 5 (signs on `4`, `5`); Subcases 3.4.2.1 and 3.4.2.2,
  paths by (21) and Lemma 3.17;
* Subcase 3.4.2.3: the entries outside the window cleaned (`clean_ind`), the entries `j`, `l` of
  depth 2 and `m` of depth 3 of Lemma 5.13, and the transfer along
  `(-1)_[α] X_[α,β] H_[j,m]` (`transfer_win`) to a state of Subcase 3.4.2.1.

Every node splits on the parity of a form in the parameters (`pat_dich`) until its step is
